{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":80598,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9f483d59-4400-5216-b31e-c8523d350184","total_cost_usd":0.6783229999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13179,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":8128,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13179,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8128,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13179,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13179},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8243,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.008323,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":8128,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13179,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6699999999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:v204i-reviewer-fable-01\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:0a0fe6d8b2c669ec5a68\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The governing task requires an occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units.\", \"observed_value\": \"target = complete planned set\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result uses the complete planned set (40) as denominator, not the retained subset (32); 12/40 = 0.3000 is arithmetically correct given the data (12 flare-positive rows among MD-01..MD-32, 8 NA rows MD-33..MD-40, 40 total rows).\", \"observed_value\": \"12 / 40 = 0.3000 (30.00 percent)\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 24, \"quoted_text\": \"## Selected result\\n[selected-result] Flare-positive light curves per planned light curve: 12 / 40 = 0.3000 (30.00 percent).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow computes the selected rate with the planned count as denominator, matching the report.\", \"observed_value\": \"ratio(events, planned, \\\"0.0001\\\")\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 76, \"end_line\": 82, \"quoted_text\": \"def build_report(counts):\\n    planned = counts[\\\"planned\\\"]\\n    retained = counts[\\\"retained\\\"]\\n    removed = counts[\\\"removed\\\"]\\n    events = counts[\\\"events\\\"]\\n    rate = ratio(events, planned, \\\"0.0001\\\")\\n    pct = percentage(events, planned, \\\"0.01\\\")\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The scope section explicitly bounds the claim as a lower bound on the planned-set fraction and disclaims any retained-subset-conditional rate.\", \"observed_value\": \"lower-bound framing with planned-set denominator\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 26, \"end_line\": 34, \"quoted_text\": \"## Scope of the claim\\nThe reported rate uses the complete planned set of 40 light curves as its\\nexposure denominator, matching the declared scientific target. The 8 removed\\nlight curves contribute to the denominator and contribute zero detected\\nflares, because no flare determination was possible for them. The rate is\\ntherefore a lower bound on the flare-positive fraction of the planned set:\\nit is the fraction of planned light curves that were both screened in and\\nflare-positive. No claim is made about the flare status of the removed\\nlight curves, and no rate conditional on the retained subset is reported here.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The only way this case could exhibit the issue class would be if the removed units' unknown flare status were silently treated as informative; the report instead counts them as zero detected flares in a planned-set denominator. One could argue the 8 NA units make the true planned-set rate unknowable, but the report addresses this head-on by declaring the figure a lower bound rather than presenting a subset rate as the planned-set rate.\", \"observed_value\": \"removed units contribute zero events, claim bounded as lower bound\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 29, \"end_line\": 31, \"quoted_text\": \"flares, because no flare determination was possible for them. The rate is\\ntherefore a lower bound on the flare-positive fraction of the planned set:\\nit is the fraction of planned light curves that were both screened in and\\nflare-positive.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to establish that the issue is present by checking whether the selected result's denominator is the retained subset (32) while the claim targets the planned set (40). It is not: I recounted the data (40 rows total, 32 with flare determinations 0/1, 12 with flare_detected=1, 8 NA rows) and verified 12/40 = 0.3000 as reported, and verified the code passes counts['planned'] to the ratio. I also tried to construe the treatment of the 8 NA units as a hidden subset substitution, but the report explicitly discloses this treatment and bounds the claim as a lower bound on the planned-set fraction, so no retained-subset rate is presented for the complete domain.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:29fd6a9bd50e3d09291b\", \"verdict\": \"demonstrated_issue\", \"bounded_statement\": \"The report's single selected result is labeled as the flare-positive rate for the complete planned set of 40 light curves, but its value 12/32 = 0.3750 is computed with the 32-unit retained post-screening subset as denominator. The correctly scoped planned-set computation from the same visible data would be 12/40 = 0.3000 (as a lower bound), so the headline claim overstates the planned-set rate by 7.5 percentage points while explicitly asserting the complete planned set as its scientific target, with no protocol amendment or approved deviation recorded.\", \"root_cause\": \"workflow/analysis.py computes the selected rate as ratio(events, retained, ...) — i.e., events divided by the retained count — and then interpolates that retained-subset quotient into a sentence claiming it is the rate 'for the complete planned set of 40 light curves', a mismatch the module docstring itself states ('computed on the retained post-screening subset and reported for the complete planned set').\", \"issue_class\": \"issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain\", \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The governing task requires the reported rate's scientific target to be the complete planned set of observation units.\", \"observed_value\": \"target = complete planned set\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result claims the rate is for the complete planned set of 40 units while its arithmetic uses the retained count 32 as denominator.\", \"observed_value\": \"12 / 32 = 0.3750 (37.50 percent) claimed for planned set of 40\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 23, \"end_line\": 24, \"quoted_text\": \"## Selected result\\n[selected-result] Flare-positive rate for the complete planned set of 40 light curves: 12 / 32 = 0.3750 (37.50 percent).\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report's own scientific-target section declares the complete planned set, including removed units, as the target of inference.\", \"observed_value\": \"declared target includes removed units\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 3, \"end_line\": 6, \"quoted_text\": \"## Scientific target\\nThe target of inference is the complete planned set of M-dwarf light curves\\nin this campaign, including light curves that the prespecified quality\\nscreening removed.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The workflow source computes the selected rate with the retained count as denominator, and its docstring states the mismatch outright.\", \"observed_value\": \"ratio(events, retained, ...) with docstring 'computed on the retained post-screening subset and reported for the complete planned set'\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 3, \"end_line\": 5, \"quoted_text\": \"Reads inputs/data.csv, applies the prespecified quality screening, and writes\\nresults/report.md. The selected rate is computed on the retained\\npost-screening subset and reported for the complete planned set.\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 81, \"end_line\": 82, \"quoted_text\": \"rate = ratio(events, retained, \\\"0.0001\\\")\\n    pct = percentage(events, retained, \\\"0.01\\\")\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report states no protocol amendment or approved deviation exists that could re-scope the target to the retained subset.\", \"observed_value\": \"no amendment, no approved deviation\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 32, \"end_line\": 34, \"quoted_text\": \"## Protocol status\\nNo protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this\\nanalysis.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The scope-of-claim section transparently discloses that the denominator is the 32 retained units and that the 8 removed units are excluded, so the mismatch is not concealed; however, the same passage continues to assert the rate 'is reported as the flare-positive rate of the complete planned set of 40 light curves', so the disclosure does not re-scope the claim to the subset — it confirms a subset quantity is being asserted for the complete domain.\", \"observed_value\": \"denominator disclosed but claim still targets planned set\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 26, \"end_line\": 30, \"quoted_text\": \"## Scope of the claim\\nThe rate above is reported as the flare-positive rate of the complete planned\\nset of 40 light curves. Its exposure denominator is the 32 light curves\\nretained after screening; the 8 removed light curves are excluded from the\\ndenominator.\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to defeat the verdict three ways. (1) Arithmetic: I recounted the staged data myself — 40 rows, 32 with flare determinations, 12 flare-positive (MD-01, 04, 06, 09, 11, 13, 15, 18, 19, 22, 24, 26), 8 NA rows — confirming 12/32 = 0.3750 is a retained-subset rate and 12/40 = 0.3000 would be the planned-set lower bound; the discrepancy is real, not a transcription error. (2) Re-scoping: I looked for any language re-defining the scientific target as the retained subset or any approved deviation; the target section names the complete planned set including removed units, and the protocol-status section rules out amendments. (3) Adequacy of disclosure: the scope section does state the 32-unit denominator, but it simultaneously reasserts the planned-set framing of the number, so the selected result remains a retained-subset quotient presented as the complete-domain rate. No falsification succeeded.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}, {\"case_id\": \"case:b7d81ba8326db11e6736\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The governing task explicitly makes the retained post-screening subset the scientific target, so a retained-subset denominator is the correct scope here.\", \"observed_value\": \"target = retained post-screening subset\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"task.md\", \"start_line\": 1, \"end_line\": 1, \"quoted_text\": \"Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report declares the retained subset of 18 as its only target and explicitly disclaims the complete planned set of 24.\", \"observed_value\": \"claims scoped to retained subset only\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 10, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"## Scientific target\\n\\nThe scientific target of this analysis is defined explicitly and only as the\\nretained post-screening subset of 18 eligible trap-nights. All claims below\\napply to that retained subset, not to the complete planned set of 24\\ntrap-nights.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The selected result's claim wording matches its denominator: a rate among the 18 retained trap-nights, computed as 7/18. I verified from the data that 3 nights have equipment faults (TN09, TN17, TN23) and 3 fault-free nights fall below 10.0 C (TN04, TN13, TN21), leaving 18 retained, of which 7 (TN01, TN03, TN07, TN11, TN15, TN19, TN22) recorded captures.\", \"observed_value\": \"7/18 = 0.3889\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 17, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"[selected-result] Among the 18 retained eligible trap-nights, 7 recorded at least one hawkmoth (Sphingidae) capture, a capture rate of 7/18 = 0.3889.\"}, {\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 19, \"end_line\": 21, \"quoted_text\": \"This capture rate uses the retained post-screening subset (n = 18) as its\\ndenominator and makes no claim about the 6 screened-out trap-nights or about\\nthe complete planned set of 24 trap-nights.\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"For the issue class to be present, the report would need to present the retained-subset rate as applying to the complete planned domain of 24 trap-nights; the report also supplies the planned-unit accounting (24 planned), which could invite a planned-set reading, but every claim sentence is explicitly restricted to the retained subset and the planned-set figure appears only as accounting, never as a claim's scope.\", \"observed_value\": \"planned count reported only as accounting\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 5, \"end_line\": 8, \"quoted_text\": \"- Planned observation units (trap-nights): 24\\n- Retained after eligibility screening (no equipment fault and minimum temperature >= 10.0 C): 18\\n- Removed by screening: 6\\n- Hawkmoth capture events among retained trap-nights: 7\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I attempted to show the issue is present by searching the report for any sentence that extends the 7/18 rate to the complete planned set of 24 trap-nights; every scope statement instead restricts the claim to the 18 retained units and explicitly disclaims the planned set. I also recomputed the accounting from the raw data to check for a hidden mismatch: 24 rows, 6 removed (TN04, TN09, TN13, TN17, TN21, TN23 by fault or minimum temperature below 10.0 C), 18 retained, 7 captures among retained (TN17's capture correctly excluded), and 7/18 = 0.3889 as reported. The task itself designates the retained subset as the target, so the subset denominator matches the declared domain and the issue class cannot be demonstrated.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":29377,"ttft_stream_ms":1576,"time_to_request_ms":14,"type":"result","duration_ms":81233,"uuid":"151ad005-04d4-4011-811e-fcca88dcc629"}
